            {
                "entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                "word": "bowser",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a7d810c0-65f3-4608-92e6-93e5d5f24713",
                        "entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bowsers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "586a2abf-5f6a-3d06-b73b-5e62d2a5407a",
                        "entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fuel metering/delivery pump at a filling station."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f92c67d0-01ee-4bac-b66c-739aec181965",
                                "sense_id": "586a2abf-5f6a-3d06-b73b-5e62d2a5407a",
                                "text": "‘Kids are breaking into the service station bowsers at night, draining out the dregs of petrol from the bowser hoses, wandering the streets sniffing petrol from Coke bottles all night,’ he said[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8017c9d8-ac2d-4dba-b9d8-722cf14ec101",
                                "sense_id": "586a2abf-5f6a-3d06-b73b-5e62d2a5407a",
                                "text": "I needed at least fifteen litres more petrol in my tank to reach the next major settlement and, unlike China, there were no shiny new gas stations here with bowsers of different types of petrol to choose from, nor were there pretty young gas girls in nice uniforms ready to fill ‘er up – in fact there were no gas stations here at all; petrol was bought and sold strictly off market in private transactions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7f79cd8-ff1b-4d16-9b2c-84ad19241de4",
                                "sense_id": "586a2abf-5f6a-3d06-b73b-5e62d2a5407a",
                                "text": "2010, David Nichols, Green Fields, Brown Fields, New Fields, footnote citing 1926 report, page 309,\nThe Moree Municipal Council decided to devote the revenue derived from the rent of the bowser petrol pumps within the municipality for this year, which amounted to forty guineas."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad5554ae-d1d8-3efb-ba7a-02620304d9e3",
                        "entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A road vehicle (often a trailer) for the transport of liquid fuel, particularly aviation fuel at an airfield."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7661ed11-2070-469c-b138-81b3ec17ebe6",
                                "sense_id": "ad5554ae-d1d8-3efb-ba7a-02620304d9e3",
                                "text": "The bowsers then go out to the aircraft and supply them with petrol."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e351925-0f93-460e-a1f9-bbe5a705a1ae",
                                "sense_id": "ad5554ae-d1d8-3efb-ba7a-02620304d9e3",
                                "text": "By the time No 43 Sqn was given permission to land it was quite dark, and so to assist the pilots in what were to be difficult night landings two petrol bowsers were parked to ‘illuminate’ the runway with their dim blackout headlights. Perhaps, all things considered, the use of petrol bowsers for this particular task was not exactly wise."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4bbdb3ca-ee4c-3a46-8e5d-bdd0033b40c6",
                        "entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mobile water tank deployed to distribute fresh water in emergency situations where the normal system of piped distribution has broken down or is insufficient."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7592b3e6-a356-4224-be34-9910e34189d8",
                                "sense_id": "4bbdb3ca-ee4c-3a46-8e5d-bdd0033b40c6",
                                "text": "Mr. Deputy Speaker, Sir, as hon. Shidie has said, there is no water bowser in Garissa and he categorically said that there is a water bowser to supply water to the people of Kulan. Could he give the registration number of this water bowser which is supplying water to the people of Kulan?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5462a6d-40c6-4ca8-834a-93eb3cda1079",
                                "sense_id": "4bbdb3ca-ee4c-3a46-8e5d-bdd0033b40c6",
                                "text": "The water bowser needed filling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f47da667-0b99-4227-bb30-6c70fc82ea7c",
                                "sense_id": "4bbdb3ca-ee4c-3a46-8e5d-bdd0033b40c6",
                                "text": "2010, P. Dissanayake, N. Weragala, V. Smakhtin, Environmental Flow Assessment: Recent Examples from Sri Lanka, Alexandra Evans, K. Jinapala (editors), Proceedings of the National Conference on Water, Food Security and Climate Change in Sri Lanka, Volume 2, page 29,\nDue to increasing levels of water pollution arising from low flows, water becomes unsuitable for bathing during this period and is satisfied by bowser water supply."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d0e6178-8894-3daf-a631-feb07a44269e",
                        "entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A buffoon or imbecile."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ireland",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1d4405ed-bce1-4155-b505-dc5f753681c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                        "source_sense_description": "fuel pump",
                        "target_lang_word": "pompe (à essence)",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab95e53e-2a4d-4f20-9982-f499d3d90be9",
                        "source_entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
                        "source_sense_description": "fuel pump",
                        "target_lang_word": "pompe à essence",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pompe à essence",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "513b7b4f-1905-325b-aad1-0644fc9a6354",
                                        "entry_id": "d97b482c-341f-3d9b-a548-e4ec0df0f591",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Équipement qui permet au moyen d’un tuyau souple de remplir le réservoir d’un véhicule en carburant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a61e79e-ab09-41f4-9d53-4c45acd91fb7",
                                                "sense_id": "513b7b4f-1905-325b-aad1-0644fc9a6354",
                                                "text": "En face de lui, Maigret voyait une petite épicerie dont il finissait par connaître tous les bocaux. Plus loin, la pompe à essence du garage, pompe qui ne devait être là que pour garnir, car on servait toujours l’essence en bidons !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6f10077-1eab-4e43-b25a-1b90a4117066",
                                                "sense_id": "513b7b4f-1905-325b-aad1-0644fc9a6354",
                                                "text": "16 novembre 44 – Il me fait du bien comme une pompe à essence. J'ai fait mon plein d’optimisme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2519c737-acd4-4a12-b089-2d8aeb827783",
                                                "sense_id": "513b7b4f-1905-325b-aad1-0644fc9a6354",
                                                "text": "Hopper a apporté certaines modifications : il a déplacé vers le fond le poteau qui porte l’enseigne et a rajouté à sa place, entre les deux pompes à essence, la pompe à air qui se trouvait sur le côté du bâtiment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6789a88-ce4e-32a8-8cab-67fbb741726b",
                                        "entry_id": "d97b482c-341f-3d9b-a548-e4ec0df0f591",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mécanisme d’un moteur à explosion qui alimente le carburateur en essence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ac35c04-543d-4995-a4f0-f00c404afbde",
                                                "sense_id": "c6789a88-ce4e-32a8-8cab-67fbb741726b",
                                                "text": "Pompe à essence. — La pompe de beaucoup la plus employée à l’heure actuelle est la pompe A.M. La disposition d’ensemble est encore la même, en général, que ci-dessus. La pompe aspire l’essence du réservoir, situé plus bas que le carburateur. Elle la refoule généralement dans une nourrice ou dans un autre réservoir situé plus haut que le carburateur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a47f4589-894e-3e81-826c-f14cdbfa2fe2",
                                        "entry_id": "d97b482c-341f-3d9b-a548-e4ec0df0f591",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Station-service."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "metonymically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14e30bf6-51c0-4094-a932-0db2464949b5",
                                                "sense_id": "a47f4589-894e-3e81-826c-f14cdbfa2fe2",
                                                "text": "« Moi, j’ai deux emplois, explique Rachel, 43 ans. Je travaille 13 heures par jour, six jours sur sept, pour essayer d’arriver à quelque chose. Et je gagne 1.200 euros par mois. Donc, c’est bon, les taxes, y en a marre ! Ça baisse toujours pour les riches et ça augmente toujours pour les pauvres. Monsieur Macron, c’est pas lui qui va à la pompe à essence ! Qu’il commence à faire ses déplacements en train ou à pied, et après on verra. »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3aa6b00f-1eb5-4295-8dae-e3bb175a9e9c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b1f39d96-499c-30fd-8ec1-5b33f5522b8f",
